  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity building Female entrepreneurs, Tanzania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to support female-led scale-ups in various sectors, including horticulture, poultry, spices, aquaculture, and potatoes in Tanzania. The project aims to identify the most significant constraints and gender-related barriers that hinder the growth of their businesses. By providing training on specific topics, female entrepreneurs are empowered, connected to new national, regional or international markets, and have better access to finance, which increases their chances of scaling up. The outcomes of this project will strengthen the agricultural value chain in Tanzania, leading to improved regional and international export opportunities. This program continues the Embassy-supported SheFound Brilliant Accelerator Program for Tanzanian women-led SMEs. This program focuses on personal development, finance management, and business development.</narrative>
  </description>
